IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-dates`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06.
--
-- LAYER 1, PART 2: regulations 2 and 3 (prisoners; persons remanded in custody).
-- Written from the text alone and from no one's point of view.
--
-- The rule is tested day by day, because regulation 2(1) speaks of "any period
-- during which the person is a prisoner" and regulation 2(2)(c)(ii) turns on a day.

§ `Part 2: Prisoners`

§§ `Regulation 2: facts about the person's custody`

-- Facts a witness could state about a person on a given day (no rule is needed to
-- state them). "Legal custody" is the Regulations' own phrase and is taken as stated.
DECLARE Custody HAS
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Regulation 2(2): who is a prisoner`

-- Gloss: (a) is held in custody because of criminal proceedings, in Great Britain or
-- abroad; (b) has escaped or is otherwise unlawfully at large, in Great Britain or
-- abroad; (c) is a prisoner transferred to hospital under the Mental Health Act 1983,
-- up to the release date the Secretary of State certifies; (d) is detained in Scotland
-- under section 136 of the 2003 Act.
-- src:30 | (a) a prisoner in Great Britain or elsewhere who is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings;
@ref Regulation 2(2)(a) (src:30)
GIVEN custody IS A Custody
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 2(2)(a): the person is a prisoner in custody` custody MEANS
    custody's `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings`

-- src:31 | (b) a prisoner in Great Britain or elsewhere who is unlawfully at large;
@ref Regulation 2(2)(b) (src:31)
GIVEN custody IS A Custody
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 2(2)(b): the person is a prisoner unlawfully at large` custody MEANS
    custody's `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large`

-- Paragraph (c)(ii) says "on or before the day which the Secretary of State certifies
-- to be the person's release date (if any)". Where there is no certified release date
-- there is no day to be after, so (c)(ii) is read as satisfied (NOTES.md, fork F5).
-- src:32 | (c) a prisoner in Great Britain who is being detained—
-- src:33 | (i) under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983 (removal to hospital of persons serving sentences of imprisonment etc) ; and
-- src:34 | (ii) on or before the day which the Secretary of State certifies to be the person's release date (if any) within the meaning in section 50(3) of that Act ;
@ref Regulation 2(2)(c) (src:32-34)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      custody IS A Custody
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 2(2)(c): the person is a prisoner detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` day custody MEANS
        custody's `the person is in Great Britain`
    AND custody's `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983`
    AND CONSIDER custody's `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST releaseDate THEN day AT MOST releaseDate

-- src:35 | (d) a prisoner in Great Britain who is being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003 (transfer of prisoners for treatment of mental disorder) .
@ref Regulation 2(2)(d) (src:35)
GIVEN custody IS A Custody
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 2(2)(d): the person is a prisoner detained under section 136 of the Scottish Act` custody MEANS
        custody's `the person is in Great Britain`
    AND custody's `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003`

§§ `Regulation 2(3): custody outside Great Britain that would not have made a prisoner in Great Britain`

-- Gloss: someone held abroad who, in the same circumstances in Great Britain, would
-- not have been a prisoner is not a prisoner under (a) or (b).
-- src:36 | (3) Where a person outside Great Britain is a prisoner within paragraph (2)(a) or (b) and, in similar circumstances in Great Britain, the person would not have been a prisoner, the person is not a prisoner within paragraph (2)(a) or (b).
@ref Regulation 2(3) (src:36)
GIVEN custody IS A Custody
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 2(3): the person is outside Great Britain and would not have been a prisoner there` custody MEANS
        NOT (custody's `the person is in Great Britain`)
    AND (   `regulation 2(2)(a): the person is a prisoner in custody` custody
         OR `regulation 2(2)(b): the person is a prisoner unlawfully at large` custody)
    AND custody's `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner`

-- "Except where paragraph (3) applies, a person is a prisoner ... where the person is (a) ... (d)".
-- src:29 | (2) Except where paragraph (3) applies, a person is a prisoner for the purposes of paragraph (1) where the person is—
@ref Regulation 2(2) (src:29)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      custody IS A Custody
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` day custody MEANS
        NOT (`regulation 2(3): the person is outside Great Britain and would not have been a prisoner there` custody)
    AND (   `regulation 2(2)(a): the person is a prisoner in custody` custody
         OR `regulation 2(2)(b): the person is a prisoner unlawfully at large` custody
         OR `regulation 2(2)(c): the person is a prisoner detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` day custody
         OR `regulation 2(2)(d): the person is a prisoner detained under section 136 of the Scottish Act` custody)

§§ `Regulation 3: persons remanded in custody`

-- The kinds of sentence that regulation 3(2) lists, and the two facts regulation 3(3)
-- asks about a sentence imposed abroad.
DECLARE KindOfSentence IS ONE OF
    `a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings`
    `a sentence of detention where the provisions mentioned in regulation 2(2)(c)(i) or (d) apply`
    `a suspended sentence within the meaning in section 286 of the Sentencing Code`
    `any other sentence`

DECLARE Sentence HAS
    `the kind of sentence` IS A KindOfSentence
    `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:40 | (2) Subject to paragraph (3), the described sentences for the purposes of paragraph (1) are—
-- src:41 | (a) a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings;
-- src:42 | (b) a sentence of detention where the provisions mentioned in regulation 2(2)(c)(i) or (d) apply;
-- src:43 | (c) a suspended sentence within the meaning in section 286 of the Sentencing Code (suspended sentences of imprisonment).
-- src:44 | (3) A sentence described in paragraph (2)(a) which is imposed outside Great Britain is not a described sentence for the purposes of paragraph (1) if, in similar circumstances in Great Britain, a sentence described in paragraph (2)(a) would not have been imposed.
@ref Regulation 3(2) and (3) (src:40-44)
GIVEN sentence IS A Sentence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 3(2): the sentence is a described sentence` sentence MEANS
    CONSIDER sentence's `the kind of sentence`
    WHEN `a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings` THEN
        NOT (       sentence's `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain`
                AND sentence's `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed`)
    WHEN `a sentence of detention where the provisions mentioned in regulation 2(2)(c)(i) or (d) apply` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a suspended sentence within the meaning in section 286 of the Sentencing Code` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other sentence` THEN FALSE

-- Everything the rule for a day needs about the person.
DECLARE PrisonStatus HAS
    `the person's custody on the day` IS A Custody
    `the person is remanded in custody for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a sentence later imposed for the offence, if any` IS A MAYBE Sentence

-- Gloss: a person on remand is not within regulation 2(1) unless they are later
-- sentenced, for the same offence, to one of the sentences in paragraph (2).
-- Whether the remand period then counts backwards is not stated (NOTES.md, fork F6).
-- src:39 | (1) Where a person is remanded in custody for an offence, regulation 2(1) does not apply unless a sentence described in paragraph (2) is later imposed on the person for the offence.
@ref Regulation 3(1) (src:39)
GIVEN status IS A PrisonStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 3(1): regulation 2(1) does not apply because the person is remanded in custody` status MEANS
        status's `the person is remanded in custody for an offence`
    AND NOT (CONSIDER status's `a sentence later imposed for the offence, if any`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST sentence THEN `regulation 3(2): the sentence is a described sentence` sentence)

§§ `Regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid`

-- src:28 | (1) Subject to regulation 3, a person is not to be paid a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act (state pension) for any period during which the person is a prisoner who is mentioned in paragraph (2).
@ref Regulation 2(1) (src:28)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      status IS A PrisonStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid for the day` day status MEANS
        `regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` day (status's `the person's custody on the day`)
    AND NOT (`regulation 3(1): regulation 2(1) does not apply because the person is remanded in custody` status)

§§ `Regulation 2(4): regulation 13 and the rights to relevant benefits`

-- "Relevant benefits" is not defined in these Regulations, and the paragraph does not say
-- what replaces the minimum of regulation 13 in the determination it mentions
-- (NOTES.md, fork F7). The encoding records only the stated effect: regulation 13
-- does not have effect in that determination.
-- src:37 | (4) In determining a person’s rights to relevant benefits for the purposes of this regulation, regulation 13 of the State Pension Regulations 2015 (minimum number of qualifying years), and any provisions in Northern Ireland which correspond to that regulation, shall not have effect.
@ref Regulation 2(4) (src:37)
`regulation 2(4): regulation 13 has effect when determining rights to relevant benefits for regulation 2` MEANS FALSE
